Known Bugs
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. /MODUNLOAD causes cores:

   If a module file is modified before being unloaded, /MODUNLOAD (and
   /MODRELOAD) may cause a core. This is an OS-level issue with how shared
   libraries are handled and cannot be fixed at the application level.

   Workaround: remove or rename the old module file before copying the new
   one into place. /MODUNLOAD will then work correctly.

   Alternatively, build with --enable-static to link all modules statically.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. Latent buffer overflow in substitution_parse() (deferred):

   In src/substitution.c, after copying a substitution value:

       rb_strlcpy(bptr, val->value, IRCD_BUFSIZE - (bptr - buf));
       bptr += strlen(val->value);

   rb_strlcpy() correctly truncates to the space remaining in buf, but
   bptr is then advanced by the full, untruncated strlen(val->value). If
   a value is longer than the space left in buf, bptr moves past
   buf + IRCD_BUFSIZE; the loop exits on its bound check and the trailing
   "*bptr = '\0'" writes out of bounds.

   This is pre-existing (inherited from ratbox/charybdis), not a
   regression. Fix: advance bptr only by the number of bytes actually
   written, e.g. bptr += strlen(bptr) after the copy, or clamp to the
   remaining space. Reachability depends on how long a val->value a
   caller can supply.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Report bugs at: https://github.com/dcorbe/ircd-phatbox/issues

Include a gdb backtrace and keep your binaries, modules, and core file
in case developers need more information.
